# pyscan ignore list — vulnerability IDs intentionally suppressed.
# Each entry MUST carry a justification. Review periodically.

# GHSA-3936-cmfr-pm3m — black 24.10.0 ReDoS in cache-file naming via the
# `--python-cell-magics` option. Black is a dev/CI-only formatter; the flag is
# never set from untrusted input in our pipeline, so this is not exploitable.
# Bumping to the fixed 26.x line would re-flow the entire codebase (a separate,
# deliberate change). Tracked for a future formatter upgrade.
GHSA-3936-cmfr-pm3m

# GHSA-wj6h-64fc-37mp — python-ecdsa 0.19.2 is vulnerable to a Minerva
# timing attack, but no patched release exists. The package is transitive via
# python-jose's optional ECDSA support; Skyulf authentication uses asymmetric
# cryptography-backed algorithms rather than ECDSA signing.
GHSA-wj6h-64fc-37mp
PYSEC-2026-1325
